A [Tauri 2](https://tauri.app) plugin for the lacodda line.
Scaffolded with [lyrn](https://github.com/lacodda/lyrn).

## Install

Two halves, published together and versioned together.

```console
$ cargo add tauri-plugin-{{ name }}
$ pnpm add tauri-plugin-{{ name }}-api
```

Register the Rust half on the builder:

```rust
tauri::Builder::default()
    .plugin(tauri_plugin_{{ lib_name }}::init())
    .run(tauri::generate_context!())
    .expect("error while running the application");
```

Grant the permission set in `src-tauri/capabilities/default.json`:

```json
{ "permissions": ["{{ name }}:default"] }
```

Then call it from the webview:

```ts
import { {{ command_camel }} } from 'tauri-plugin-{{ name }}-api'

const answer = await {{ command_camel }}()
```

